什么？

313
00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:39.660
So-
所以——

314
00:14:39.660 --> 00:14:40.000
How long?
多久？

315
00:14:40.080 --> 00:14:41.180
You had it for like a night?
你才开了不到一晚？

316
00:14:41.340 --> 00:14:41.960
One day.
一天。

317
00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:43.180
You went one place.
你只去了一个地方。

318
00:14:44.480 --> 00:14:48.800
And Kevin Nealon drove a car eerily similar to that.
而且凯文·尼隆开的车和那辆车惊人地相似。

319
00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.560
I'm not saying he had anything to do with the robbery, but it was kind of weird.
我不是说这抢劫案跟他有关，但这确实有点奇怪。

320
00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:56.280
But my first car was a Volkswagen Bug.
不过我的第一辆车是大众甲壳虫。

321
00:14:56.380 --> 00:14:59.860
Are you going to go to first car or first car when you got an extra paycheck?
你是要讲第一辆车，还是讲拿到额外薪水后买的第一辆车？

322
00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:01.820
Me?
我吗？

323
00:15:02.340 --> 00:15:03.040
No, but you are.
不，是你。

324
00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:03.880
We know your story.
我们都知道你的故事。

325
00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:04.600
We know my story.
我们都知道我的故事。

326
00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:05.020
Yeah.
是啊。

327
00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:05.400
David?
大卫？

328
00:15:05.840 --> 00:15:06.120
You got it.
你说对了。

329
00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:11.380
Oh, I had my fair share because I do like cars, but my neck gives me trouble.
噢，我买过不少车，因为我确实喜欢车，但我的脖子总出毛病。

330
00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.400
So every time I get a car I love, it just starts.
所以每次我买到喜欢的车，毛病就开始了。

331
00:15:13.560 --> 00:15:14.760
It's just too painful.
实在太痛苦了。

332
00:15:14.940 --> 00:15:18.220
And like Jenna said, when you're starting and stopping all day, it's not like you live
就像珍娜说的，当你整天都在走走停停时，这可不像住在

333
00:15:18.220 --> 00:15:21.680
in the Midwest and you can floor it and there's big parking lots.
中西部，你可以一路狂飙，而且到处都是大停车场。

334
00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:25.240
Like when you go to Wendy's in Arizona, there's like 300 parking spots.
比如你在亚利桑那去温蒂汉堡，那里有三百个停车位。

335
00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.040
And when you go here, there's one at Kmart.
而在这里，凯马特超市只有一个车位。

336
00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:29.940
And you go, are we all sharing this?
你会想，我们都要共用这一个吗？

337
00:15:29.940 --> 00:15:34.920
You can't believe when you get to LA how little there's some businesses have absolutely no
你刚到洛杉矶时简直不敢相信，有些商家的停车位少到

338
00:15:34.920 --> 00:15:35.280
parking.
根本没有。

339
00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:37.640
So I don't know what we're supposed to do.
所以我不知道我们该怎么办。

340
00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:43.600
So that kind of threw me and I realized I didn't need big fancy cars.
所以那件事让我很受挫，我意识到我根本不需要什么豪车。

341
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:45.940
I could just tell people I had them.
我只要告诉别人我有就行了。

342
00:15:46.020 --> 00:15:46.680
I didn't really need them.
我其实并不需要它们。

343
00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:50.020
My first car was also a manual transmission.
我的第一辆车也是手动挡的。

344
00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:50.940
Oh boy.
天哪。

345
00:15:51.280 --> 00:15:58.680
And my left foot would like truly ache at the end of like driving all day in LA because
在洛杉矶开了一整天车后，我的左脚真的会疼得要命，因为

346
00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:03.320
there was, you were constantly just going like in and out of third and fourth gear.
你得不停地在三档和四档之间来回切换。

347
00:16:03.520 --> 00:16:06.200
There was like, you never made it to fifth gear in this car.
在那辆车里，你根本就挂不上五档。

348
00:16:06.440 --> 00:16:08.380
God, no one has a stick anymore.
天哪，现在没人开手动挡了。

349
00:16:08.820 --> 00:16:13.020
No, it's a, it's a, you know, this was the cheapest car.
不，那是，那是，你知道，那是当时最便宜的车。

350
00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:15.280
Like the manual transmission was the cheapest car.
手动挡的车就是最便宜的。

351
00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:16.440
My dad's very practical.
我爸非常务实。

352
00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.180
He was like, you'll get this car.
他当时说，你就买这辆车。

353
00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:20.080
I'll teach you how to drive it.
我会教你怎么开。

354
00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:22.120
This is all you need.
这就足够了。

355
00:16:22.120 --> 00:16:23.380
You don't need any frills.
你不需要任何花哨的东西。

356
00:16:23.880 --> 00:16:24.180
Yeah.
是啊。

357
00:16:24.880 --> 00:16:25.840
In St. Louis.
在圣路易斯。

358
00:16:26.320 --> 00:16:26.720
Yeah.
没错。

359
00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:30.280
So do you, you've been to St. Louis, I bet.
你也去过吧，我敢打赌你肯定去过圣路易斯。

360
00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:32.240
I'm going to St. Louis to do a show.
我要去圣路易斯做一场演出。

361
00:16:32.740 --> 00:16:35.140
Have you had Emo's Pizza in St. Louis?
你在圣路易斯吃过Emo's披萨吗？

362
00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:37.400
Uh, Emo's Pizza in St. Louis?
呃，圣路易斯的Emo's披萨？

363
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.460
No, but I, I, I like it as a town.
没有，但我，我，我挺喜欢那个城市的。

364
00:16:40.620 --> 00:16:41.380
I like walking around.
我喜欢在那儿到处走走。

365
00:16:41.560 --> 00:16:46.560
I like that stadiums are really close in, you know, not in the-
我喜欢那里的体育场离市区很近，你知道，不是在那个……

366
00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.320
Jenna, do you know what Chesterfield is?
珍娜，你知道切斯特菲尔德在哪吗？

367
00:16:49.140 --> 00:16:50.480
Chesterfield is where I grew up.
切斯特菲尔德是我长大的地方。

368
00:16:50.660 --> 00:16:51.620
Oh, is it really?
哦，真的吗？

369
00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:54.600
Chesterfield is where my family lives now.
切斯特菲尔德是我家人现在住的地方。

370
00:16:55.180 --> 00:16:55.680
Uh-oh.
噢，糟糕。

371
00:16:55.680 --> 00:17:03.260
Yeah, I actually grew up, uh, in, like, Manchester slash Chesterfield in an unincorporated area.
是啊，我其实是在曼彻斯特和切斯特菲尔德之间的一个非建制地区长大的。

372
00:17:03.940 --> 00:17:06.000
Uh, but yeah, Chesterfield for sure.
不过，确实是切斯特菲尔德。

373
00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:06.260
Why?
怎么了？

374
00:17:06.660 --> 00:17:08.260
Because that's where I'm going for my tour.
因为那是我巡演要去的地方。

375
00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:14.180
And they said, I was with Nikki, uh, Glazer this weekend and she's from St. Louis.
他们说，我这周末和妮基·格雷泽在一起，她是圣路易斯人。

376
00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:16.820
And she goes, why don't they put on your tour St. Louis?
她说，为什么你的巡演名单上没有圣路易斯？

377
00:17:17.060 --> 00:17:19.100
No one, it says Chesterfield.
没人写圣路易斯，上面写的是切斯特菲尔德。

378
00:17:19.180 --> 00:17:20.140
And I go, oh, I don't know.
我说，哦，我不知道。

379
00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:21.200
I don't even know where I'm going.
我甚至都不知道我要去哪儿。

380
00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:24.320
I mean, if you're from St. Louis, you know what Chesterfield is.
我是说，如果你是圣路易斯人，你就知道切斯特菲尔德是什么地方。

381
00:17:24.320 --> 00:17:24.460
You'll know?
你会知道的，对吧？

382
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:25.240
Okay, good.
好的，那就好。

383
00:17:25.300 --> 00:17:27.360
Yeah, it's not like, yeah, it's not downtown.
是啊，它不像，对，它不在市中心。

384
00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:28.940
I mean, St. Louis is downtown.
我是说，圣路易斯是指市中心。

385
00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:30.120
You're going to be in the burbs.
你要去的是郊区。

386
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:30.740
You're in the suburbs.
你在郊区。

387
00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:31.640
That's fine with me.
我没意见。

388
00:17:31.740 --> 00:17:33.040
And, uh, I think it's a great place.
而且，我觉得那是个好地方。

389
00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:33.640
I've been there before.
我以前去过那里。

390
00:17:33.720 --> 00:17:34.460
I think it's new.
我觉得那是新的。

391
00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.780
Uh, anyway, we'll set up comps for everyone you know from high school.
呃，总之，我们会为你所有高中认识的人安排赠票。

392
00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:39.080
Other than that.
除此之外。

393
00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:39.560
Great.
太棒了。

394
00:17:40.060 --> 00:17:40.420
Great.
太棒了。

395
00:17:42.260 --> 00:17:42.960
You know, Dana.
你知道的，达娜。

396
00:17:42.960 --> 00:17:44.120
Be careful what you say.
说话小心点。

397
00:17:44.520 --> 00:17:47.540
My high school ladies are going to come out for your show.
我的高中女同学们会来看你的演出。

398
00:17:47.800 --> 00:17:48.980
Yeah, it's, it's super fun.
是啊，那真的，真的很有趣。

399
00:17:49.600 --> 00:17:50.680
Dana and I had a question.
达娜和我有个问题。

400
00:17:51.200 --> 00:17:54.060
I'll tell Dana a little pre-question that you don't know.
我会先告诉达娜一个你不知道的小问题。

401
00:17:54.140 --> 00:17:54.480
All right.
好的。

402
00:17:54.620 --> 00:17:57.460
Let's try to keep our guests off balance.
我们试着让嘉宾们措手不及。

403
00:17:57.620 --> 00:17:59.720
Like with questions she's not asked all the time.
比如问一些她平时不会被问到的问题。

404
00:17:59.860 --> 00:18:00.200
Oh yeah.
哦，没错。

405
00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:00.880
We're here to watch.
我们是来旁观的。

406
00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:02.060
We want to surprise you.
我们想给你个惊喜。

407
00:18:02.200 --> 00:18:03.240
She's going to come out here dizzy.
她出来的时候肯定会晕头转向的。

408
00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:03.840
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

409
00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:04.580
So.
那么。

410
00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:04.960
Great.
太棒了。

411
00:18:05.420 --> 00:18:06.860
Everyone loves that in an interview.
每个人在采访中都喜欢这样。

412
00:18:07.140 --> 00:18:11.700
I thought of doing this with Dana and then I called Jenna, right?
我本来想和达娜一起做这个，然后我给珍娜打了电话，对吧？

413
00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:12.620
Jenna, do you remember this?
珍娜，你还记得吗？

414
00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:13.940
Yes, of course.
是的，当然记得。

415
00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:14.300
Yes.
是的。

416
00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:15.500
And you were very sweet.
你当时非常贴心。

417
00:18:15.640 --> 00:18:19.220
You took the call and you kind of walked me through how it works and what you did.
你接了电话，还耐心地给我讲解了它是如何运作的，以及你是怎么做的。

418
00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:23.080
And it really gave me a little boost to say, this might be fun.
这真的给了我一点鼓励，让我觉得，这可能会很有趣。

419
00:18:23.440 --> 00:18:25.520
And if it has to be a day and it has to be, that's fine.
如果非得选一天，那就选一天，没关系。

420
00:18:25.660 --> 00:18:25.800
Whatever.
无所谓。

421
00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:25.880
Whatever.
无所谓。

422
00:18:27.360 --> 00:18:32.320
And so, and then Dana had a question of, do you really need a partner?
然后达娜问了一个问题，你真的需要搭档吗？

423
00:18:32.900 --> 00:18:35.320
Has it ever gone through your mind?
你有没有想过这个问题？

424
00:18:35.780 --> 00:18:37.760
I could have done this by myself.
我本可以自己做这件事的。

425
00:18:38.020 --> 00:18:39.480
And then the money doubles.
而且钱还能翻倍。

426
00:18:39.800 --> 00:18:41.420
Has that ever gone through your mind?
你有没有想过这个问题？

427
00:18:43.360 --> 00:18:44.860
Or maybe Angela.
或者也许是安吉拉。

428
00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:47.060
But that.
但那个嘛。

429
00:18:47.320 --> 00:18:49.280
Dana and I think about that all day, every day.
达娜和我整天都在想这个问题，每天都在想。

430
00:18:49.280 --> 00:18:53.100
People always ask us forever, why, you know, why us?
人们总是没完没了地问我们，为什么，你知道，为什么是我们？

431
00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:53.700
Why now?
为什么是现在？

432
00:18:53.880 --> 00:18:54.640
Are you really friends?
你们真的是朋友吗？

433
00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:55.420
Do you get that?
你们常被问到这个吗？

434
00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:58.620
I mean, you guys are famously really close friends.
我是说，你们可是出了名的好闺蜜。

435
00:18:58.740 --> 00:18:59.900
But with Spade and I, I was like, what?
但对于我和斯派德，我就在想，什么？

436
00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:02.720
The Tommy boy guy and the Williams world guy?
那个演《小淘气》的家伙和演《威廉姆斯世界》的家伙？

437
00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:03.220
I don't know.
我不知道。

438
00:19:03.480 --> 00:19:03.720
Yeah.
是啊。

439
00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:04.880
Yeah.
是啊。

440
00:19:05.060 --> 00:19:08.780
Well, I mean, also because Angela and I were frenemies on The Office.
嗯，我是说，也是因为安吉拉和我在《办公室》里是“相爱相杀”的关系。

441
00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.460
Our characters were not friends.
我们的角色并不是朋友。

442
00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:14.840
And people are always very surprised to learn that we are best friends in real life.
人们总是很惊讶地发现，我们在现实生活中是最好的朋友。

443
00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:18.800
Um, I could not have done the podcast without her.
嗯，没有她我根本做不了这个播客。

444
00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:23.940
I am all like structure and order and spreadsheets.
我这个人满脑子都是结构、秩序和电子表格。

445
00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:31.100
My version of Office Ladies podcast would be very informative, but also way less entertaining.
我一个人做的《办公室女士》播客会非常有信息量，但会少很多娱乐性。

446
00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:39.240
So Angela brings all of the like funny and all of the quirky and all of like the weird observations.
所以安吉拉带来了所有的趣味性、古怪感以及那些奇奇怪怪的观察。

447
00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.100
So we're actually, we're a pretty good pair.
所以我们实际上是一对很好的搭档。

448
00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:48.300
Yeah, I think that's smart that you did that because there is kind of safety in numbers.
是啊，我觉得你这样做很聪明，因为人多确实比较有安全感。

449
00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:52.020
Dana is way better at this.
达娜在这方面比我强多了。

450
00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.660
And, uh, I don't think I could do myself.
而且，呃，我觉得我一个人做不来。

451
00:19:55.060 --> 00:20:00.240
I think Dana really, really drives it and makes it easier to, uh, do it for me.
我觉得达纳真的非常、非常地推动了这一切，让我做起来轻松多了。

452
00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:00.560
Except today.
除了今天。

453
00:20:00.820 --> 00:20:05.820
But jokingly, it's fun to joke around with him too, because he's a funny guy, obviously.
但开玩笑地说，跟他打趣也很有意思，因为他显然是个风趣的人。

454
00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.640
And, uh, we have a good time with that.
而且，呃，我们在一起玩得很开心。

455
00:20:07.780 --> 00:20:09.600
And I think you guys have a real friendship.
我觉得你们之间有真正的友谊。

456
00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:15.120
So people like to hear that you're friends, even though it doesn't seem like it on the show.
所以大家很喜欢听到你们是朋友，尽管在节目里看起来不像。

457
00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:17.300
You guys, I love your podcaSt.
你们好，我超爱你们的播客。

458
00:20:17.540 --> 00:20:21.500
Like I, you have no idea how excited I am to be on your podcast right now.
真的，你们无法想象我现在能上你们的播客有多激动。

459
00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:22.440
I listen to you guys.
我一直在听你们的节目。

460
00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:24.540
I think you are so good together.
我觉得你们配合得太好了。

461
00:20:25.100 --> 00:20:29.920
Um, Dana, I can't believe I, you're talking to me right now.
嗯，达纳，我简直不敢相信，你现在在跟我说话。

462
00:20:29.960 --> 00:20:31.940
Uh, that's kind of blowing my mind.
呃，这让我感到有点不可思议。

463
00:20:31.940 --> 00:20:34.560
And I'm a huge Saturday Night Live nerd.
而且我还是个超级《周六夜现场》迷。

464
00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:42.940
The greatest part about being on The Office and being on NBC was that I got to breathe the same air as Saturday Night Live people.
出演《办公室》并在NBC工作最棒的一点就是，我能和《周六夜现场》的人呼吸同一片空气。

465
00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:48.720
This is like that we would have to be at the same corporate parties together.
就像是我们得一起参加同样的商业派对一样。

466
00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.380
And I was a total groupie.
我当时完全是个小迷妹。

467
00:20:51.620 --> 00:20:53.500
That is who I gravitated toward.
那就是我会被吸引过去的人。

468
00:20:53.860 --> 00:20:56.320
It was just the cooleSt.
那简直太酷了。

469
00:20:56.580 --> 00:20:58.400
And, but that's going way back.
不过那都是很久以前的事了。

470
