00:27:50.310 --> 00:27:52.930
And they painted my body with makeup.
他们还在我身上涂了化妆品。

633
00:27:53.070 --> 00:27:55.370
I mean, I felt, like, so covered.
我是说，我觉得自己被裹得严严实实的。

634
00:27:55.610 --> 00:27:56.530
It was crazy.
太疯狂了。

635
00:27:56.530 --> 00:27:59.710
He has to go and grab your boobs through your stuff, but it's, like, that kind of thing.
他得隔着那些东西去抓你的胸部，但就是那种感觉。

636
00:27:59.770 --> 00:28:02.010
You can't even feel it because you've got 18 layers of.
你根本感觉不到，因为你穿了十八层衣服。

637
00:28:02.410 --> 00:28:02.710
Yeah.
是啊。

638
00:28:02.790 --> 00:28:04.250
It's, like, I was wearing body armor.
就像我穿了防弹衣一样。

639
00:28:04.550 --> 00:28:09.590
So, I was kind of, like, maybe, like, wink when you grab them because I can feel nothing.
所以我当时就想，也许你抓的时候给我使个眼色吧，因为我什么都感觉不到。

640
00:28:10.310 --> 00:28:13.490
This was three dates intimacy coordinators.
那会儿哪有什么亲密协调员啊。

641
00:28:13.670 --> 00:28:15.110
There was no one there.
当时现场根本没人。

642
00:28:15.870 --> 00:28:16.810
There was no.
根本没有。

643
00:28:16.930 --> 00:28:18.130
It was just, okay.
当时就是，好吧。

644
00:28:18.470 --> 00:28:19.990
It was just, like, here's what we're doing.
就是有人说，我们要拍这个。

645
00:28:20.130 --> 00:28:21.450
It was just a director going, let's do this.
就是导演喊一声，我们开始吧。

646
00:28:21.670 --> 00:28:22.010
Yes.
是的。

647
00:28:22.690 --> 00:28:23.090
Exactly.
没错。

648
00:28:24.310 --> 00:28:25.350
Was Swartzen in that?
斯沃森演了吗？

649
00:28:25.350 --> 00:28:27.010
Yeah, do you know Nick Swartzen, that little fool?
是啊，你认识尼克·斯沃森那个小傻瓜吗？

650
00:28:27.450 --> 00:28:27.890
Yes.
认识。

651
00:28:28.130 --> 00:28:28.950
Yes, he was.
是的，他是。

652
00:28:29.330 --> 00:28:30.190
Oh, my God.
天哪。

653
00:28:30.690 --> 00:28:31.690
We are friends with Nick.
我们和尼克是朋友。

654
00:28:31.870 --> 00:28:34.510
And, you know, it's a real roller coaster, Jenna.
而且，你知道，这真的像坐过山车一样，珍娜。

655
00:28:34.530 --> 00:28:35.030
I'll tell you that.
我得跟你说。

656
00:28:35.030 --> 00:28:35.570
It is.
确实如此。

657
00:28:35.730 --> 00:28:39.630
I found him lovely on the film, but what do I know?
我觉得他在电影里很可爱，但我又懂什么呢？

658
00:28:39.910 --> 00:28:40.790
No, he's great.
不，他很棒。

659
00:28:40.810 --> 00:28:41.690
He's so funny.
他太搞笑了。

660
00:28:42.050 --> 00:28:42.650
Hall Pass.
《嘿咻卡》。

661
00:28:43.730 --> 00:28:46.130
We haven't even gotten to the goddang office.
我们甚至还没聊到该死的《办公室》呢。

662
00:28:46.910 --> 00:28:48.990
I have a question about the office.
我有个关于《办公室》的问题。

663
00:28:50.050 --> 00:28:50.710
What is it?
什么问题？

664
00:28:50.850 --> 00:28:53.990
The question is for you and your partner.
这个问题是问你和你搭档的。

665
00:28:55.730 --> 00:28:58.490
Rewatching all these episodes and talking about them.
重温所有这些剧集并谈论它们。

666
00:28:58.970 --> 00:28:59.490
Yeah.
是啊。

667
00:28:59.650 --> 00:29:03.890
What, how is your perception, if it at all, changed about the show?
你们对这部剧的看法有没有什么改变，如果有的话，是什么？

668
00:29:03.990 --> 00:29:05.410
Or what did you learn about the show?
或者说你们对这部剧有了什么新的认识？

669
00:29:05.550 --> 00:29:12.890
Or if anything, because it is now officially a phenomenon in the way it travels around and then explodes again.
或者说有没有什么变化，因为它现在正式成为了一种现象，以这种方式传播开来，然后再次爆发。

670
00:29:12.890 --> 00:29:13.730
It's evergreen.
它经久不衰。

671
00:29:14.390 --> 00:29:16.590
And it's a, it's a unique show.
而且它是一部独特的剧集。

672
00:29:17.190 --> 00:29:23.150
And, um, uh, yesterday I was watching, um, the office with Ricky Gervais.
嗯，昨天我在看瑞奇·热维斯版的《办公室》。

673
00:29:23.750 --> 00:29:24.210
Very different.
非常不同。

674
00:29:24.330 --> 00:29:29.730
I mean, it, it, you know, you say it came from that office, but it went, it, it has its own complete original thing.
我的意思是，你知道，你说它源自那个版本的《办公室》，但它走出了自己的路，它有自己完全原创的东西。

675
00:29:29.870 --> 00:29:31.630
Greg Daniels, one of the great writers.
格雷格·丹尼尔斯，伟大的编剧之一。

676
00:29:31.630 --> 00:29:36.750
So what did you guys, what, what do you feel about that thing after doing hundreds of podcasts?
那么你们在做了几百期播客之后，对这件事有什么感觉？

677
00:29:37.030 --> 00:29:40.270
Did you, did you go through every episode at some point?
你们是不是在某个阶段重温了每一集？

678
00:29:40.650 --> 00:29:40.790
Yeah.
是的。

679
00:29:40.870 --> 00:29:44.230
Every single episode, all 201 episodes.
每一集，全部201集。

680
00:29:44.570 --> 00:29:48.790
Um, and then a lot of, um, interviews with cast and crew.
嗯，还有很多对演职人员的采访。

681
00:29:48.950 --> 00:29:49.330
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

682
00:29:49.810 --> 00:29:50.070
Um.
嗯。

683
00:29:50.910 --> 00:29:51.330
Writers.
编剧们。

684
00:29:51.750 --> 00:29:52.850
Writers, exactly.
编剧们，没错。

685
00:29:52.850 --> 00:29:59.650
Um, my biggest takeaway from having rewatched it was that it's really good the whole time.
嗯，我重温之后最大的收获是，它全程都非常精彩。

686
00:30:00.130 --> 00:30:07.610
Because I think there was this lore, especially among the cast and the creatives, that maybe we, like, hit our peak in season three.
因为我觉得当时有一种说法，特别是在演职人员和创作团队中，认为我们可能在第三季达到了巅峰。

687
00:30:07.910 --> 00:30:08.070
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

688
00:30:08.070 --> 00:30:09.130
Or season four.
或者是第四季。

689
00:30:09.450 --> 00:30:17.230
And also this belief that, like, the two seasons after Steve left, we were just treading water and maybe they weren't as good.
还有一种观点认为，史蒂夫离开后的那两季，我们只是在原地踏步，可能没那么好。

690
00:30:17.230 --> 00:30:25.190
But when I watched everything, like, some of my favorite episodes were in seasons eight and nine after Steve had left.
但当我重温所有剧集时，我发现我最喜欢的一些剧集其实是在史蒂夫离开后的第八季和第九季。

691
00:30:25.310 --> 00:30:27.810
Like, there were still these amazing storylines.
比如，依然有那些精彩的故事线。

692
00:30:28.410 --> 00:30:37.250
And also, I have to say now, when I look back, my, some of my favorite episodes were also in seasons four through six.
而且我必须说，现在回过头来看，我最喜欢的一些剧集也出现在第四到第六季。

693
00:30:37.470 --> 00:30:39.330
Like, Dinner Party was season four.
比如，《晚宴》是在第四季。

694
00:30:39.610 --> 00:30:43.010
Michael Scott Paper Company, that whole arc was in season five.
《迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司》，整个那一章是在第五季。

695
00:30:43.230 --> 00:30:45.190
And that, like, just great TV.
那真的是非常棒的电视节目。

696
00:30:45.190 --> 00:30:45.770
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

697
00:30:45.950 --> 00:30:52.770
And, um, but yeah, I think, you know, some of the award nominations stopped after season three.
嗯，不过是的，我想，你知道，一些奖项提名在第三季之后就停止了。

698
00:30:52.770 --> 00:30:57.890
So I think maybe we got in our heads and thought, oh, I guess we're not creating as great.
所以我认为也许我们当时钻了牛角尖，觉得，哦，看来我们创作得没那么好了。

699
00:30:57.890 --> 00:31:00.250
I think that just happens no matter what.
我觉得无论如何这都会发生。

700
00:31:00.590 --> 00:31:02.530
Yeah, you're not the new shiny object anymore.
是啊，你不再是那个新鲜出炉的宠儿了。

701
00:31:02.870 --> 00:31:02.920
Yeah, yeah, exactly.
对，对，没错。

702
00:31:02.990 --> 00:31:03.870
And they kind of slow down.
而且它们节奏会慢下来。

703
00:31:03.870 --> 00:31:04.090
That's a nice thing.
那感觉挺好的。

704
00:31:04.270 --> 00:31:09.610
I mean, when you're watching yourself and you're watching a thing and then you come on and stuff and it's something you did years ago.
我是说，当你看着自己，看着某个东西，然后你出场了之类的，那是你多年前做过的事情。

705
00:31:09.610 --> 00:31:16.190
Do you ever sometimes, because you sound like you're a normal actor, comedian, that's sort of like a little self-critical.
你有没有过，因为听起来你像个正常的演员、喜剧演员，那种有点自我批判的感觉。

706
00:31:16.290 --> 00:31:16.790
How was I?
我表现得怎么样？

707
00:31:17.110 --> 00:31:20.470
Do you ever kind of look at yourself in a scene and go, damn, I nailed that.
你有没有在某个场景里看着自己，然后想，天哪，我演得太棒了。

708
00:31:20.850 --> 00:31:22.310
Why did I feel insecure?
我为什么会感到不安呢？

709
00:31:22.530 --> 00:31:24.290
Or what's that like?
或者那种感觉是什么样的？

710
00:31:24.290 --> 00:31:26.410
Um, I mean, I have both reactions.
嗯，我是说，这两种反应我都有。

711
00:31:26.650 --> 00:31:29.910
Sometimes I watch it and I'm like, I'll never do work that good again.
有时我看着它，心想，我再也演不出那么好的作品了。

712
00:31:30.290 --> 00:31:31.350
Shit, that was great.
该死，那真是太棒了。

713
00:31:32.110 --> 00:31:41.050
But then there's other scenes where I just cringe, where I'm like, oh, God, I remember how I struggled with that and I couldn't do it.
但也有其他场景让我感到尴尬，我会想，天哪，我记得当时演得有多吃力，我根本做不到。

714
00:31:41.150 --> 00:31:42.970
And now here it is for everyone to see.
而现在它就在那儿，供所有人观看。

715
00:31:43.410 --> 00:31:45.390
And I guess I just have to move on.
我想我只能继续前行了。

716
00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:46.810
So I've had both reactions.
所以我两种反应都有过。

717
00:31:46.810 --> 00:31:54.110
And I don't know the complete specifics of this, but you, it, first of all, it is, it was always an ensemble.
我不太清楚这方面的具体细节，但首先，它一直都是一部群戏。

718
00:31:54.430 --> 00:32:00.170
How great Carell is in that part is, is, you know, everybody knows that, but it always was an ensemble.
卡瑞尔在那个角色里有多棒，大家都知道，但它一直都是一部群戏。

719
00:32:00.450 --> 00:32:09.610
And so many people came out of it now have these long careers, but, um, it's, um, I forgot my train of thought.
现在很多人从那部剧里走出来，都有了很长的职业生涯，但是，嗯，我忘了我刚才想说什么了。

720
00:32:09.790 --> 00:32:09.910
Sorry.
抱歉。

721
00:32:10.850 --> 00:32:13.030
I was, do you ever have something in my head?
我刚才，你脑子里有没有过什么东西？

722
00:32:13.430 --> 00:32:23.690
And Jenna, when you can watch it and say, I was in the pocket because sometimes you watch it and you go, you're just in, in the pocket of going, this is a great scene.
还有珍娜，当你看着它并说，我当时状态正好，因为有时你看着它，你会觉得，你正处于那种状态，觉得这是一场很棒的戏。

723
00:32:23.950 --> 00:32:25.810
This whole idea of this episode's working.
这一整集的效果都很好。

724
00:32:25.970 --> 00:32:31.510
And when they whip the camera back, get a great look, whip back to you, perfect timing, get a great look.
当他们把镜头甩回去，捕捉到一个很棒的表情，再甩回给你，时机完美，捕捉到一个很棒的表情。

725
00:32:31.630 --> 00:32:36.290
And when you see it, you go, cause you know, you can only feel the camera when you're shooting and you don't really know.
当你看到它时，你会想，因为你知道，拍摄时你只能感觉到摄像机，你并不真正知道。

726
00:32:36.510 --> 00:32:38.550
And then you go, God, they nailed that.
然后你会想，天哪，他们拍得太好了。

727
00:32:38.730 --> 00:32:39.570
Boom, boom, edited.
砰，砰，剪辑好了。

728
00:32:39.570 --> 00:32:50.070
Well, everything about this is just, that's why people really get, uh, enchanted by, I mean, and also just your face is so part of the office and it's so cute.
嗯，关于这一切，这就是为什么人们真的会，呃，被它吸引，我是说，而且你的脸也是《办公室》的一部分，而且太可爱了。

729
00:32:50.110 --> 00:32:53.270
And they always cut to you and you all, and you have these little storylines.
他们总是切到你，你们有这些小故事线。

730
00:32:53.370 --> 00:32:55.610
It's really, I see why people get hooked on it.
真的，我明白为什么人们会沉迷其中了。

731
00:32:55.670 --> 00:32:58.670
No matter when you turn it on, you can just grab any episode.
无论你什么时候打开它，你都可以随便看任何一集。

732
00:32:58.670 --> 00:33:03.530
I remember what I forgot, which is, was how much, if any, improvisation was there?
我记起我忘了什么了，那就是，如果有的话，即兴创作有多少？

733
00:33:03.750 --> 00:33:10.970
Because it comes off very improvisational in totem, but I know there wasn't completely improvised.
因为它整体上看起来非常即兴，但我知道它并非完全即兴。

734
00:33:11.150 --> 00:33:12.390
I know that's a pretty cool word, right?
我知道那是个很酷的词，对吧？

735
00:33:12.790 --> 00:33:16.010
So were you allowed to kind of go, you guys, could I try this?
所以你们被允许说，嘿，伙计们，我能试试这个吗？

736
00:33:16.290 --> 00:33:19.250
You know, do you mind if I do, you know, that kind of stuff?
你知道，我不介意我做，你知道，那种事情？

737
00:33:20.090 --> 00:33:21.770
Yeah, it was really collaborative.
是的，这真的很有协作性。

738
00:33:21.770 --> 00:33:26.810
And, um, you know, so many of the writers were also actors on the show.
而且，嗯，你知道，很多编剧也是剧中的演员。

739
00:33:26.890 --> 00:33:33.290
So they were with us and they would be sometimes pitching alternate jokes right there on the set.
所以他们和我们在一起，有时会在片场直接提出替代的笑话。

740
00:33:33.490 --> 00:33:34.070
That's kind of fun, yeah.
那挺有趣的，是吧。

741
00:33:34.070 --> 00:33:35.030
So that was neat.
所以那很棒。

742
00:33:35.290 --> 00:33:40.710
And we did a lot of improvising, but I don't know how much of it actually made the cut.
我们做了很多即兴表演，但我不知道其中有多少真正被剪进去了。

743
00:33:40.890 --> 00:33:42.810
We, we got to play and have fun.
我们有机会去玩，去享受乐趣。

744
00:33:42.810 --> 00:33:54.350
But I would say like 90% of what you see on the screen was written on the page down to like, um, they would write in ellipses for our speech.
但我会说，屏幕上你看到的90%的内容都是写在剧本上的，甚至精确到，嗯，他们会在我们的台词里写上省略号。

745
00:33:54.410 --> 00:34:00.650
Like, so you knew to kind of pause because they knew they were going to whip the camera during that pause.
这样你就知道要停顿一下，因为他们知道他们要在那个停顿期间甩动摄像机。

746
00:34:00.790 --> 00:34:02.370
And so they could get back to you.
这样他们就能回到你身上。

747
00:34:02.470 --> 00:34:11.250
So there was a very elaborate choreography of whipping the camera a little too late so that it seemed, and you'd have to get the handles.
所以有一种非常复杂的编排，就是把摄像机甩得稍微晚一点，这样看起来，而且你必须得有那些衔接镜头。

748
00:34:11.250 --> 00:34:14.710
So it seemed like the crew, yeah, they didn't quite do it right, yeah.
所以看起来像是剧组，是的，他们没完全做对，是吧。

749
00:34:15.130 --> 00:34:15.910
Yes, exactly.
是的，完全正确。

750
00:34:16.230 --> 00:34:24.950
And so a lot of times when we would do a rehearsal, they would say, Jenna, will you give a handle before your next line to, so we have time for that camera whip?
所以很多时候当我们排练时，他们会说，珍娜，你能在下一句台词前给一个衔接镜头吗，这样我们就有时间进行那个摄像机甩动了？

751
00:34:25.230 --> 00:34:28.950
So that would be, we would add things like, um, well.
所以就是，我们会加入一些，嗯，类似这样的东西。

752
00:34:29.250 --> 00:34:30.070
They'd find you.
他们会找到你。

753
00:34:30.190 --> 00:34:31.530
So that they could find you.
这样他们就能找到你。

754
00:34:31.750 --> 00:34:32.030
Yeah.
是啊。

755
00:34:32.190 --> 00:34:33.290
Like in the right timing.
就像在合适的时机那样。

756
00:34:34.050 --> 00:34:34.450
But, um.
但是，嗯。

757
00:34:34.610 --> 00:34:36.430
So great, but it also seems very real.
太棒了，而且感觉非常真实。

758
00:34:36.430 --> 00:34:46.610
A lot of the nonverbal acting and those cutaways to a character that isn't saying a line, but just sort of nonverbally doing some kind of attitude and stuff.
很多非语言的表演，还有那些切到某个没在说话的角色的镜头，他们只是通过非语言的方式表现出某种态度之类的。

759
00:34:46.870 --> 00:34:50.310
It, it, it was immediately just felt so new.
它，它，它立刻就让人感觉非常新颖。

760
00:34:50.490 --> 00:34:51.910
I, I'm not going to say fresh.
我，我不想说“新鲜”这个词。

761
00:34:52.230 --> 00:34:59.470
David would use that word a lot, but immediately, I think for comedians as well, uh, watching it going, this looks cool.
大卫很喜欢用这个词，但我觉得对喜剧演员来说，看的时候立刻就会觉得，这看起来很酷。

762
00:34:59.470 --> 00:35:00.610
This looks fun.
这看起来很有趣。

763
00:35:00.830 --> 00:35:03.130
This looks different and really funny.
这看起来很不一样，而且真的很好笑。

764
00:35:03.350 --> 00:35:04.890
It doesn't push at all.
它一点也不刻意。

765
00:35:05.270 --> 00:35:06.270
You know, it's the.
你知道，这就是。

766
00:35:06.690 --> 00:35:13.430
Well, we had, um, we had two camera operators with cameras on their shoulders and both of these guys were from Survivor.
嗯，我们有，嗯，我们有两名肩扛摄像机的摄影师，他们两个都来自《幸存者》剧组。

767
00:35:13.770 --> 00:35:21.680
So these guys had like walked through the, whatever, the wilderness with the Survivor people capturing Survivor.
所以这些人就像是和《幸存者》的人一起走过，不管是什么，荒野，拍摄《幸存者》一样。

768
00:35:21.680 --> 00:35:24.720
So this is where they came from in the documentary world.
所以这就是他们从纪录片领域带来的经验。

769
00:35:25.460 --> 00:35:32.660
And, um, camera A, Randall Einhorn, who was also our cinematographer who went on to be a director and is now, you know,
而且，嗯，A机位摄影师兰德尔·艾因霍恩，他也是我们的摄影指导，后来成为了一名导演，现在，你知道的，

770
00:35:32.740 --> 00:35:35.520
the executive producer of Abbott Elementary and all those things.
是《小学风云》的执行制片人，诸如此类的职位。

771
00:35:36.120 --> 00:35:40.300
Uh, Randall was our A camera and his job was to get all of the dialogue.
嗯，兰德尔是我们的A机位，他的工作是捕捉所有的对话。

772
00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:48.960
Um, and then Matt Sohn, he was our B camera and then his job was to get all of those things you're talking about, Dana.
嗯，然后马特·索恩，他是我们的B机位，他的工作就是捕捉你刚才说的那些东西，达娜。

773
00:35:48.960 --> 00:35:51.820
All of the acting that was happening in the background.
所有在背景中发生的表演。

774
00:35:52.260 --> 00:35:59.960
So whenever a scene was happening, we were all in the background of each other's scenes all day long on set, the full 12 hours.
所以每当有场景拍摄时，我们整整12个小时都在彼此的背景里。

775
00:36:00.740 --> 00:36:01.760
Steve Carell included.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔也不例外。

776
00:36:01.980 --> 00:36:08.340
I can't tell you how many times Steve Carell had to sit in Michael Scott's office just to be in the background of Jim and Pam looking at each other.
我无法告诉你史蒂夫·卡瑞尔有多少次不得不坐在迈克尔·斯科特的办公室里，仅仅是为了出现在吉姆和帕姆对视的背景中。

777
00:36:08.580 --> 00:36:09.060
Because we get a piece of them.
因为我们能拍到他们的一部分。

778
00:36:09.560 --> 00:36:10.960
Yeah, because we're going to see a piece.
是啊，因为我们总会拍到一部分。

779
00:36:11.060 --> 00:36:12.580
We're going to see a piece of you.
我们总会拍到你的一部分。

780
00:36:12.800 --> 00:36:15.180
It's like something we could put on a mug.
就像我们可以印在马克杯上的东西一样。

781
00:36:15.680 --> 00:36:15.860
Yeah.
是啊。

782
00:36:16.320 --> 00:36:18.860
Um, that'd be actually be a, be a great caSt.
嗯，那其实会是个，会是个很棒的……

783
00:36:18.960 --> 00:36:19.320
Gift.
礼物。

784
00:36:19.760 --> 00:36:20.900
Um, yeah.
嗯，是啊。

785
00:36:21.040 --> 00:36:27.900
And so he would grab and push in on all of the, you know, anyone who was in the background of a scene and get their reactions in real time.
所以他会抓拍并推近镜头，对准所有在场景背景里的人，实时捕捉他们的反应。

786
00:36:28.060 --> 00:36:29.560
It was such a cool way to work.
这真是一种很酷的工作方式。

787
00:36:29.900 --> 00:36:30.100
Yeah.
是啊。

788
00:36:30.240 --> 00:36:31.440
And you have to stay alive though.
但你必须保持专注。

789
00:36:31.760 --> 00:36:32.240
You do.
确实。

790
00:36:32.520 --> 00:36:32.920
Every scene.
每一场戏都是。

791
00:36:33.500 --> 00:36:35.180
But it keeps your energy up.
但这能让你保持精力充沛。

792
00:36:35.180 --> 00:36:35.420
Yeah.
是啊。

793
00:36:35.600 --> 00:36:43.700
You know, because that's the hardest thing for me about acting in movies is like the long amounts of downtime between when you're actually acting.
你知道，因为对我来说，拍电影最困难的事情就是实际表演之间那漫长的等待时间。

794
00:36:44.140 --> 00:36:47.340
It's just like, oh God, I got to ramp up again.
那种感觉就像，天哪，我又得重新进入状态了。

795
00:36:48.000 --> 00:36:48.360
Yeah.
是啊。

796
00:36:48.640 --> 00:36:58.280
And it's just, I, you know, I don't know if this is the correct way to say it, but if you feel like if you're discovering something new in the moment, it's really nice.
而且，我，你知道，我不知道这样说对不对，但如果你觉得自己在当下发现了什么新东西，那真的很棒。

797
00:36:58.280 --> 00:37:05.820
Uh, it does keep your brain alive and in traditional movies, what I was doing, um, you know, you do the three masters at seven or 8 a.m.
嗯，这确实能让你的大脑保持活跃，而在传统的电影拍摄中，我以前做的那样，嗯，你知道，你在早上七八点钟拍完三个全景镜头，

798
00:37:05.820 --> 00:37:06.380
or whatever.
或者类似的时间。

799
00:37:06.380 --> 00:37:15.420
And then by five or six o'clock you start and, oh, don't you, in the master eight hours ago, your left elbow was up and you open the corridor at this point.
然后到了五六点钟，你开始拍，噢，难道不是吗，八小时前的全景镜头里，你的左肘是抬起来的，而且你在这个时候打开了走廊的门。

800
00:37:15.640 --> 00:37:19.200
It's the antithesis of what you guys had, at least the way it felt.
这和你们当时的情况完全相反，至少感觉上是这样。

801
00:37:19.200 --> 00:37:21.640
It felt, it popped, it felt real, you know?
那种感觉，那种爆发力，感觉很真实，你懂吗？

802
00:37:21.780 --> 00:37:22.480
For sure.
确实。

803
00:37:22.480 --> 00:37:26.460
And we did not have marks, you know, those that, for people out there,
而且我们当时没有标记，你知道的，就是给外行解释一下，

804
00:37:26.640 --> 00:37:31.460
like you put tape on the ground and then you have to stand on it because that's how you're going to be in focus.
就像你在地上贴胶带，然后你必须站在上面，因为那样才能保证你在焦距内。

805
00:37:31.460 --> 00:37:39.020
But we had no marks and if the boom dipped in shot, we just kept it in because, you know, it worked in the world.
但我们没有标记，如果收音杆入镜了，我们就让它留在画面里，因为你知道，在那样的世界里这很自然。

806
00:37:39.820 --> 00:37:48.320
And, um, and when I finished, when I, you know, going back to Blades of Glory, Blades of Glory was the first big movie I did after being cast on The Office.
而且，嗯，当我拍完的时候，当我，你知道，回到《冰刀双人组》时，《冰刀双人组》是我在出演《办公室》之后拍的第一部大制作电影。

807
00:37:48.320 --> 00:37:53.500
And I repeatedly kept, um, looking down the barrel of the camera.
我总是会不自觉地，嗯，直视摄像机镜头。

808
00:37:53.700 --> 00:37:58.840
Like I would do a scene with Will and Amy and then I would like give a look to camera.
就像我和威尔还有艾米演完一场戏，然后我会看向镜头。

809
00:37:58.960 --> 00:38:00.280
I'd be like, fuck, I can't do that.
我会想，该死，我不能那样做。

810
00:38:00.420 --> 00:38:05.240
And also I suddenly had to hit a mark and I was, I was so stiff.
而且我突然得去踩标记，我当时，我太僵硬了。

811
00:38:05.240 --> 00:38:08.120
It was really stressful because I'd been in this other world.
这真的压力很大，因为我之前一直待在另一个世界里。

812
00:38:08.240 --> 00:38:14.700
You can watch when people on movies, sometimes if you ever watch, someone looks down and they walk in, look for their mark and then they look up.
你可以观察一下电影里的人，有时候如果你仔细看，有人会低头走进来，找他们的标记，然后再抬头。

813
00:38:14.880 --> 00:38:15.580
I love it.
我喜欢这个。

814
00:38:15.680 --> 00:38:16.220
It's so horrifying.
这太可怕了。

815
00:38:16.220 --> 00:38:25.560
Uh, I want to say also, I was going to say the show is fresh, but it's funny that the term fresh is stale, but also.
呃，我还想说，我本来想说这部剧很新颖，但有趣的是“新颖”这个词已经过时了，不过也是。

816
00:38:26.240 --> 00:38:27.520
I'm going to bring it back.
我要让它重获新生。

817
00:38:27.960 --> 00:38:31.700
The Office was fresh and the new one called The Paper.
《办公室》很新颖，而那部新的叫《纸业公司》。

818
00:38:32.860 --> 00:38:33.320
Yeah.
是啊。

819
00:38:33.940 --> 00:38:34.560
On Peacock.
在孔雀台播。

820
00:38:34.700 --> 00:38:35.440
Have you seen that?
你看过吗？

821
00:38:35.540 --> 00:38:36.440
Do you know much about it?
你了解多少？

822
00:38:36.860 --> 00:38:37.220
Okay.
好吧。

823
00:38:37.220 --> 00:38:39.160
I haven't seen it, but I got to go to the set.
我没看过，但我去过片场。

824
00:38:39.320 --> 00:38:45.360
Angela and I got special access to the set and, um, got to talk to all the actors.
安吉拉和我获得了特别许可进入片场，嗯，还和所有演员聊了聊。

825
00:38:45.360 --> 00:38:46.740
We got to see it.
我们看到了。

826
00:38:47.480 --> 00:38:49.940
It's really cool, but we're not allowed to say anything.
真的很酷，但我们不能透露任何内容。

827
00:38:50.400 --> 00:38:50.680
Oh yeah.
哦，是啊。

828
00:38:50.680 --> 00:38:51.860
I think that it's in the can.
我想它应该已经拍完了。

829
00:38:52.060 --> 00:38:53.340
Like they, they finished it.
就是他们，他们已经完成了。

830
00:38:53.540 --> 00:38:54.920
It comes out in September.
九月份上映。

831
00:38:55.280 --> 00:38:55.940
Oh, interesting.
哦，有意思。

832
00:38:56.680 --> 00:38:57.980
Oh, September on where?
哦，九月份在哪个平台？

833
00:38:58.880 --> 00:38:59.280
Peacock.
孔雀台。

834
00:38:59.360 --> 00:38:59.640
I don't know.
我不知道。

835
00:39:00.260 --> 00:39:00.860
Peacock, right?
孔雀台，对吧？

836
00:39:01.300 --> 00:39:01.540
Peacock.
孔雀台。

837
00:39:06.190 --> 00:39:10.950
So with John Krasinski, like the Jim and Pam narrative was, became such a big thing.
关于约翰·卡拉辛斯基，吉姆和帕姆的故事线，已经变成了一个非常重大的话题。

838
00:39:11.150 --> 00:39:16.970
I talked to some people in their early twenties today, told them I was going to interview you and on The Office.
我今天和一些二十出头的年轻人聊天，告诉他们我要采访你，还有关于《办公室》的事。

839
00:39:17.110 --> 00:39:18.510
They go, I go, she was Pam.
他们说，我说，她就是帕姆。

840
00:39:18.630 --> 00:39:19.170
Oh, Pam.
哦，帕姆。

841
00:39:19.170 --> 00:39:23.270
You know, this is like a famous character and Jim and Pam.
你知道，这是一个非常出名的角色，还有吉姆和帕姆。

842
00:39:23.570 --> 00:39:33.850
I'm just kind of curious because John Krasinski, um, I find it really, really interesting how he came up with that horror film.
我只是有点好奇，因为约翰·卡拉辛斯基，嗯，我觉得他想出那部恐怖片的方式真的非常非常有意思。

843
00:39:33.850 --> 00:39:35.390
Uh, the quiet, what was it?
呃，那个安静，叫什么来着？

844
00:39:35.450 --> 00:39:37.690
The quiet, a quiet place, quiet place.
《寂静之地》，《寂静之地》。

845
00:39:38.390 --> 00:39:45.030
And, um, it's interesting when actors just all of a sudden you see them and like, wow, this guy can really direct.
而且，嗯，当演员突然展现出那一面时很有趣，你会想，哇，这家伙真的能当导演。

846
00:39:45.290 --> 00:39:50.350
And did you see any, uh, seeds of that in him intellectually or just the way he was around?
你在他身上看到过任何这方面的苗头吗，在智力上或者他平时的表现？

847
00:39:50.430 --> 00:39:53.630
Was that a surprise to you when he came out directing?
当他开始执导时，你感到惊讶吗？

848
00:39:53.890 --> 00:39:56.190
It, it was a surprise to none of us.
我们谁都不觉得惊讶。

849
00:39:56.190 --> 00:39:57.670
Oh, I didn't think so.
哦，我猜也是。

850
00:39:57.750 --> 00:40:03.510
John, I would always say to John, I think you're going to be like our Tom Hanks.
约翰，我总是对约翰说，我觉得你会成为我们的汤姆·汉克斯。

851
00:40:03.830 --> 00:40:06.170
Like, remember how Tom Hanks did Bosom Buddies?
就像，还记得汤姆·汉克斯演过《红粉知己》吗？

852
00:40:06.470 --> 00:40:06.790
Totally.
完全记得。

853
00:40:06.970 --> 00:40:10.330
And he was like a very famous, successful TV show.
他当时演的是一部非常出名、非常成功的电视剧。

854
00:40:10.510 --> 00:40:13.830
But like when you think of Tom Hanks, you don't think of Bosom Buddies.
但当你想到汤姆·汉克斯时，你不会想到《红粉知己》。

855
00:40:13.970 --> 00:40:16.490
You think of everything else Tom Hanks has done.
你会想到汤姆·汉克斯后来演的所有其他作品。

856
00:40:16.730 --> 00:40:19.950
And I was like, I think The Office is going to be your Bosom Buddies.
我就跟他说，我觉得《办公室》会成为你的《红粉知己》。

857
00:40:20.130 --> 00:40:21.250
Like you're going places.
就是说你前途无量。

858
00:40:21.470 --> 00:40:22.550
It's very clear.
这一点非常明显。

859
00:40:22.550 --> 00:40:27.790
And did he look down at his, at the ground and go, oh, shucks, Jenna?
那他有没有低头看着地面，然后说，噢，天哪，珍娜？

860
00:40:28.410 --> 00:40:29.110
Or how did he?
还是他怎么反应的？

861
00:40:29.250 --> 00:40:29.370
He did.
他确实说了。

862
00:40:29.430 --> 00:40:29.730
He did.
他确实说了。

863
00:40:29.830 --> 00:40:30.950
He's very, yes.
他非常，是的。

864
00:40:30.970 --> 00:40:32.710
He's very humble in that way.
他在那方面非常谦虚。

865
00:40:32.850 --> 00:40:36.670
You know, like that would be, if I say that to him, that's very embarrassing to him.
你知道，如果我那样对他说，他会觉得很尴尬。

866
00:40:36.730 --> 00:40:39.930
You know, like he doesn't want to be like fussed over like that.
你知道，他不想被那样大惊小怪地对待。

867
00:40:40.190 --> 00:40:42.750
But I was like, no, it's true, mister.
但我当时就说，不，这是真的，先生。

868
00:40:43.090 --> 00:40:46.590
Well, it's a Herculean task to direct a movie.
嗯，执导一部电影是一项艰巨的任务。

869
00:40:46.790 --> 00:40:48.210
I mean, just physically and mentally.
我是说，无论是身体上还是精神上。

870
00:40:49.010 --> 00:40:49.290
But, um.
但是，嗯。

871
00:40:49.450 --> 00:40:51.270
Dana fusses over me all the time.
达娜总是对我大惊小怪的。

872
00:40:52.150 --> 00:40:52.850
Um, fusses.
嗯，大惊小怪。

873
00:40:52.910 --> 00:40:53.330
Um, yeah.
嗯，是的。

874
00:40:53.710 --> 00:40:54.450
You fussed over me.
你对我大惊小怪过。

875
00:40:54.510 --> 00:40:57.330
I want to hear more about you being a telephone psychic when you got.
我想多听听你当电话灵媒时的经历。

876
00:40:58.430 --> 00:40:59.990
Yeah, that was.
是的，那是。

877
00:41:00.390 --> 00:41:01.470
She worked as a car wash.
她在洗车店工作过。

878
00:41:01.810 --> 00:41:06.150
I did work at a car for three summers and that was my best job.
我确实在洗车店工作了三个夏天，那是我做过最好的工作。

879
00:41:06.150 --> 00:41:08.250
I worked at Long John Silver's.
我在朗约翰银鳕鱼餐厅工作过。

880
00:41:08.410 --> 00:41:09.450
That was my first job.
那是我的第一份工作。

881
00:41:10.010 --> 00:41:13.010
I worked at an ice creamery serving ice cream.
我在一家冰淇淋店卖过冰淇淋。

882
00:41:13.250 --> 00:41:15.210
And then I got the job at the car wash.
然后我就得到了洗车店的那份工作。

883
00:41:15.210 --> 00:41:22.030
All of those were on this road called Manchester Road on, um, in St. Louis out in the suburbs.
所有这些工作都在圣路易斯郊区一条叫曼彻斯特路的路上。

884
00:41:22.270 --> 00:41:24.390
And I got, I got fired from Long John Silver's.
我被朗约翰银鳕鱼餐厅解雇了。

885
00:41:24.450 --> 00:41:25.790
I got fired from the ice creamery.
我被冰淇淋店解雇了。

886
00:41:25.950 --> 00:41:30.170
And my dad would say, oh, you're just looking to get fired from every business on Manchester
我爸爸会说，噢，我看你是想把曼彻斯特路上的每家店都干到被解雇为止吧。

887
00:41:30.170 --> 00:41:30.990
Road, I guess.
我想是这样。

888
00:41:31.650 --> 00:41:35.090
Um, but the car wash stuck and that was great.
嗯，但在洗车店的工作倒是干长久了，那份工作很棒。

889
00:41:35.330 --> 00:41:36.250
That was great money.
那份工作赚的钱很多。

890
00:41:36.470 --> 00:41:39.750
I was outside just drying off the cars, you know.
我当时就在外面负责把车擦干，你知道的。

891
00:41:39.850 --> 00:41:41.850
How big are tips in that world?
那个行业的小费有多少？

892
00:41:42.030 --> 00:41:43.790
Because I try to tip well, but.
因为我尽量多给小费，但是。

893
00:41:44.250 --> 00:41:44.550
Okay.
好吧。

894
00:41:44.950 --> 00:41:45.810
This is like.
这就像是。

895
00:41:45.810 --> 00:41:46.030
Gorgeous Jenna.
美丽的珍娜。

896
00:41:46.410 --> 00:41:46.510
Yeah.
是的。

897
00:41:46.670 --> 00:41:47.850
Like back then.
就像那时候一样。

898
00:41:48.190 --> 00:41:53.810
Well, and by the way, they would always make me give the gentlemen back their cars.
顺便说一下，他们总是让我把车还给那些男士。

899
00:41:53.810 --> 00:41:59.290
Cause you have to like, yeah, you got to stand at the car and wave, you know, in your little
因为你必须，是的，你得站在车边挥手，你知道，穿着你的小短裤和小短衫，说你的车好了。

900
00:41:59.290 --> 00:42:02.910
shorts and your little cutoff shirt and like your car's ready.
你的车好了。

901
00:42:03.490 --> 00:42:09.250
Um, and I would, I would, I'm not, you know, not to brag, but I would get a five sometimes.
