你可以看这个。

1199
00:55:54.600 --> 00:55:58.160
You can go restroom and you go this and it plays even longer.
你可以去洗手间，做这做那，而且演出时间更长。

1200
00:55:59.020 --> 00:56:02.940
And just to feel like you had a grumbly stomach or your back hurts or something like, oh shit,
只要觉得肚子不舒服或者背痛什么的，就会想，糟了。

1201
00:56:03.060 --> 00:56:03.740
can I do this?
我能这样做吗？

1202
00:56:04.140 --> 00:56:05.560
Do I call in somebody?
我要叫人来吗？

1203
00:56:05.700 --> 00:56:06.520
You know, so weird.
你知道，太奇怪了。

1204
00:56:07.200 --> 00:56:14.180
I had a shooting pain in my left leg, kind of inside my left leg.
我的左腿突然一阵剧痛，好像是在左腿里面。

1205
00:56:14.340 --> 00:56:16.640
And so all of a sudden my left leg was inoperable.
然后我的左腿突然就动不了了。

1206
00:56:16.780 --> 00:56:22.900
I was playing in front of 2000 people and I was in a, and I'm like, okay, got to go with
当时我在两千人面前表演，我心想，好吧，只能硬着头皮

1207
00:56:22.900 --> 00:56:26.980
this, you know, incorporated into the act, you know, and then it worked itself out.
把它融入到表演里，你知道，后来它自己就好了。

1208
00:56:26.980 --> 00:56:29.960
What I was interested in also, besides we all do that.
除了我们都会那样做之外，我还对别的事情感兴趣。

1209
00:56:30.040 --> 00:56:30.620
I think it's great.
我觉得这很棒。

1210
00:56:30.620 --> 00:56:36.340
You have that certain show day prep, but the gentleman who is playing your father, what
你有那种演出当天的准备工作，但那位扮演你父亲的先生，他

1211
00:56:36.340 --> 00:56:36.860
is his name?
叫什么名字？

1212
00:56:37.020 --> 00:56:37.780
Fran Guinan.
弗兰·吉南。

1213
00:56:38.360 --> 00:56:43.360
So Larry David was just talking about when he does usually whatever he's doing, I don't
拉里·大卫刚才在谈论他通常做的事情，我不知道

1214
00:56:43.360 --> 00:56:44.460
know if he does standup or whatever.
他是不是在做单口喜剧之类的。

1215
00:56:44.620 --> 00:56:47.760
It's just the fatigue goes away once there's the audience, you know?
一旦面对观众，疲劳感就会消失，你知道吗？

1216
00:56:48.040 --> 00:56:51.960
And then I think in a play you're holding onto him, he's holding onto you.
而且我觉得在戏剧里，你扶着他，他扶着你。

1217
00:56:52.140 --> 00:56:57.920
And that connection can hopefully make the part of your brain going, how am I doing?
那种连接有望让大脑里那个“我表现得怎么样？”的部分安静下来。

1218
00:56:58.300 --> 00:56:59.000
How's it going?
进行得怎么样？

1219
00:56:59.000 --> 00:57:01.020
When all that go away at times, right?
当这一切有时消失的时候，对吧？

1220
00:57:01.140 --> 00:57:02.400
That's the electricity of it.
那就是其中的火花。

1221
00:57:02.500 --> 00:57:09.240
If you get so involved in the scene with your partner that it feels exhilarating, right?
如果你和搭档全身心投入到场景中，感觉会非常令人振奋，对吧？

1222
00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:13.400
When you know you're connecting and the audience is with you, that's what you live for, right?
当你感觉到你们在交流，观众也与你们同在时，那就是你活着的意义，对吧？

1223
00:57:14.480 --> 00:57:14.920
Yeah.
是的。

1224
00:57:15.040 --> 00:57:19.880
I mean, that's the dope of the whole thing of live performance.
我是说，那就是现场表演最让人上瘾的地方。

1225
00:57:20.360 --> 00:57:22.500
I mean, that's the thing we're chasing.
我是说，那就是我们所追求的东西。

1226
00:57:22.680 --> 00:57:25.440
That's the high you're chasing every time.
那是你每次都在追求的快感。

1227
00:57:25.440 --> 00:57:30.460
And even if your prep doesn't go as well as you want or you ate too much, you still always
即使你的准备工作不如预期，或者你吃得太多，你依然

1228
00:57:30.460 --> 00:57:32.680
have that possibility of that happening.
拥有那种可能性。

1229
00:57:33.520 --> 00:57:33.920
Yes.
是的。

1230
00:57:34.360 --> 00:57:34.760
Yes.
是的。

1231
00:57:35.000 --> 00:57:37.540
And also if they get something wrong, the audience doesn't know this.
而且如果他们出错了，观众是不知道的。

1232
00:57:37.760 --> 00:57:38.780
They could miss a line.
他们可能会漏掉一句台词。

1233
00:57:38.900 --> 00:57:39.640
You cover form.
你会帮着圆场。

1234
00:57:39.800 --> 00:57:43.600
There's little things that are like teamwork, things that are fun to do that you get to
有一些像团队合作一样的小事，做起来很有趣，当你

1235
00:57:43.600 --> 00:57:45.380
the end and someone's like, hey, you saved me.
演完后有人会说，嘿，你救了我。

1236
00:57:45.480 --> 00:57:46.260
I spaced out.
我刚才走神了。

1237
00:57:46.420 --> 00:57:48.640
And the audience doesn't really know what's going on.
而观众根本不知道发生了什么。

1238
00:57:48.640 --> 00:57:50.880
But you guys, you forgot a prop.
但你们知道，你们忘了拿道具。

1239
00:57:51.080 --> 00:57:52.460
There's little things that keep it alive.
这些小事让表演保持鲜活。

1240
00:57:52.460 --> 00:57:56.640
But that's kind of the fun teamwork of it all, like in a show also.
但这正是演出中那种有趣的团队合作，就像在节目里一样。

1241
00:57:57.200 --> 00:57:59.680
That happened to me during a show.
我在演出时就遇到过这种情况。

1242
00:58:01.720 --> 00:58:06.960
I did a show off Broadway and me and this other actress were on stage.
我演过一场外百老汇的戏，我和另一位女演员在台上。

1243
00:58:06.960 --> 00:58:10.960
And we're only on stage for like four lines because we don't like each other.
我们只上台说了大概四句台词，因为我们互相看不顺眼。

1244
00:58:11.140 --> 00:58:13.080
And we're waiting for the same guy.
我们在等同一个男人。

1245
00:58:13.080 --> 00:58:16.840
We like the same guy and we're waiting for him to walk in and break the tension.
我们喜欢同一个男人，我们在等他走进来打破僵局。

1246
00:58:17.060 --> 00:58:18.580
And he didn't come on stage.
但他没上台。

1247
00:58:18.900 --> 00:58:19.860
He didn't come.
他没来。

1248
00:58:20.060 --> 00:58:21.500
He just missed his entrance.
他错过了出场时间。

1249
00:58:21.900 --> 00:58:29.480
And so I started improvising, which then the playwright was like, oh, my God, I can't
所以我开始即兴发挥，后来剧作家说，天哪，我不敢

1250
00:58:29.480 --> 00:58:31.340
believe people thought I wrote those lines.
相信人们以为那些台词是我写的。

1251
00:58:31.540 --> 00:58:34.520
That was just like improvisation.
那简直就像即兴表演一样。

1252
00:58:34.640 --> 00:58:36.120
I'm like, what were we supposed to do?
我当时心想，我们该怎么办？

1253
00:58:36.180 --> 00:58:37.320
We're just sitting there.
我们只是坐在那儿。

1254
00:58:37.500 --> 00:58:39.140
No one was coming on.
没人上场。

1255
00:58:39.140 --> 00:58:43.840
And it's an art piece of you sit in silence for 12 minutes waiting while they find the
那是一件艺术作品，你得在沉默中坐上12分钟，等着他们去隔壁熟食店

1256
00:58:43.840 --> 00:58:45.140
guy at the deli next to him.
找那个家伙。

1257
00:58:45.240 --> 00:58:49.180
I like it when someone didn't silence their phone or is talking to the phone.
我喜欢有人没把手机调静音，或者对着手机说话的时候。

1258
00:58:49.300 --> 00:58:52.360
And then the actor in the Broadway show breaks character.
然后百老汇演出的演员就出戏了。

1259
00:58:52.360 --> 00:58:54.900
He's in some kind of clown suit or dresses a bear.
他穿着某种小丑服，或者打扮成一只熊。

1260
00:58:55.020 --> 00:58:57.380
I will kill you, motherfucker.
我要杀了你，你这混蛋。

1261
00:58:58.100 --> 00:59:00.460
You know, it's just that clown suit.
你知道，就是那身小丑服。

1262
00:59:00.460 --> 00:59:01.180
It's live.
这是现场直播。

1263
00:59:01.840 --> 00:59:02.100
Yeah.
没错。

1264
00:59:02.360 --> 00:59:11.620
Now, Jenna, my last thing for you is I like that when you audition for The Office, Allison
好了，珍娜，最后我想问你的是，我听说你为《办公室》试镜时，艾莉森·琼斯

1265
00:59:11.620 --> 00:59:12.920
Jones is a casting director.
是选角导演。

1266
00:59:13.060 --> 00:59:15.560
We probably all three have run into along the way.
我们三个可能都在演艺生涯中遇到过她。

1267
00:59:15.660 --> 00:59:16.160
The beSt.
她是最好的。

1268
00:59:16.420 --> 00:59:18.240
Said, dare to bore me.
她说，敢于让我感到无聊。

1269
00:59:18.380 --> 00:59:19.140
I think that's interesting.
我觉得这很有意思。

1270
00:59:19.580 --> 00:59:20.540
I read that.
我读到过那段话。

1271
00:59:20.740 --> 00:59:26.480
I like that because most people are trying to give you the biggest pizzazz of a lifetime
我喜欢这个说法，因为大多数人在试镜时都想展现出

1272
00:59:26.480 --> 00:59:27.180
in an audition.
一生中最精彩、最引人注目的表演。

1273
00:59:27.180 --> 00:59:32.020
Well, I had been auditioning for Allison for about five years before The Office.
嗯，在《办公室》之前，我已经为艾莉森试镜大约五年了。

1274
00:59:32.400 --> 00:59:35.500
I got my first speaking role on a television show.
我拿到的第一个有台词的电视角色。

1275
00:59:35.780 --> 00:59:39.140
It was Spin City, the Charlie Sheen years.
是《政界小人物》，查理·辛主演的那几年。

1276
00:59:39.660 --> 00:59:42.480
And I had three lines as a waitress.
我演一个女服务员，只有三句台词。

1277
00:59:42.800 --> 00:59:46.360
And then I would she would bring me in for other little things.
后来她会找我演一些其他小角色。

1278
00:59:46.860 --> 00:59:47.300
Sure.
当然。

1279
00:59:47.920 --> 00:59:53.340
And finally, when it was time for her to cast The Office, I had a good enough relationship
最后，当她要为《办公室》选角时，我和她关系已经足够好，

1280
00:59:53.340 --> 00:59:56.440
with her that I could say, hey, Allison, do you have any advice?
所以我可以问她，嘿，艾莉森，你有什么建议吗？

1281
00:59:56.440 --> 00:59:58.180
I really want this one.
我真的很想要这个角色。

1282
00:59:58.320 --> 01:00:04.360
And she said, yeah, my advice is don't come in looking hot, like don't come in all done
她说，好的，我的建议是别打扮得太性感，别把自己

1283
01:00:04.360 --> 01:00:04.680
up.
收拾得太精致。

1284
01:00:04.820 --> 01:00:11.340
And by the way, usually the note was, OK, you're playing a pediatric nurse, but like
顺便说一下，通常的要求是，好吧，你演一个儿科护士，但要

1285
01:00:11.340 --> 01:00:15.020
hot or like you're playing a school teacher, but like really hot.
性感一点，或者你演一个学校老师，但要非常性感。

1286
01:00:15.280 --> 01:00:17.900
So like usually the note was look hot.
所以通常的要求都是要看起来性感。

1287
01:00:18.240 --> 01:00:19.320
Mortician, but hot.
殡仪员，但要性感。

1288
01:00:19.640 --> 01:00:20.800
But super hot.
而且要超级性感。

1289
01:00:20.980 --> 01:00:22.100
Like she's really, really hot.
就像她真的、真的非常性感那样。

1290
01:00:22.100 --> 01:00:26.860
And I'm like, OK, so she was like, don't come in like looking hot.
我当时心想，好吧，所以她的意思是，别打扮得太性感。

1291
01:00:27.140 --> 01:00:28.260
Don't come in with a bunch of makeup.
别化太浓的妆。

1292
01:00:28.520 --> 01:00:28.920
Overdone.
别用力过猛。

1293
01:00:29.080 --> 01:00:29.180
Yeah.
没错。

1294
01:00:29.300 --> 01:00:30.100
We want real people.
我们需要真实的人。

1295
01:00:30.400 --> 01:00:34.240
And then she said, we're going to have you improvise during the audition.
然后她说，我们要让你在试镜时进行即兴表演。

1296
01:00:34.640 --> 01:00:37.220
And my advice is dare to bore me.
我的建议是，敢于让我感到无聊。

1297
01:00:37.940 --> 01:00:39.880
And I was like, OK, great.
我当时心想，好的，太棒了。

1298
01:00:40.040 --> 01:00:42.760
So I went in and I read the scene.
于是我进去读了剧本。

1299
01:00:42.940 --> 01:00:45.760
And then Greg Daniels said, OK, we're going to improvise.
然后格雷格·丹尼尔斯说，好的，我们要开始即兴表演了。

1300
01:00:45.860 --> 01:00:48.960
I'm going to just ask you some questions as if I'm a documentary filmmaker.
我会以纪录片导演的身份问你一些问题。

1301
01:00:48.960 --> 01:00:56.620
Um, and I had that note in my head and he said, um, do you like being a receptionist
嗯，我当时脑子里有那个念头，然后他说，嗯，你喜欢做前台吗？

1302
01:00:56.620 --> 01:00:56.920
here?
在这里？

1303
01:00:57.740 --> 01:01:01.080
And I just paused and I said nothing.
我停顿了一下，什么也没说。

1304
01:01:03.090 --> 01:01:06.090
And then I said, no.
然后我说，不喜欢。

1305
01:01:09.110 --> 01:01:10.570
And that's all I said.
我就说了这些。

1306
01:01:10.590 --> 01:01:11.350
That's funny.
真有意思。

1307
01:01:11.690 --> 01:01:17.430
Because I thought it would be funnier to watch me think of all the things I wasn't going
因为我觉得，看着我思考那些我没说出口的话，比直接说出来更有趣。

1308
01:01:17.430 --> 01:01:20.150
to say than to say any of them.
比说出其中任何一句都更有趣。

1309
01:01:20.790 --> 01:01:24.090
And then also, though, she's like a deeply honest person.
而且，她也是个非常诚实的人。

1310
01:01:24.170 --> 01:01:27.250
So she can't lie and say she does like it.
所以她没法撒谎说她喜欢这份工作。

1311
01:01:27.290 --> 01:01:29.490
But she's also not going to say any more.
但她也不会多说半个字。

1312
01:01:30.010 --> 01:01:30.450
Wow.
哇。

1313
01:01:30.590 --> 01:01:32.170
And I think that's what got me the job.
我觉得正是这一点让我得到了这份工作。

1314
01:01:32.490 --> 01:01:33.990
Greg told me that's what got me the job.
格雷格告诉我，就是因为这个我才被录用的。

1315
01:01:34.230 --> 01:01:35.390
That is so cool.
太酷了。

1316
01:01:35.490 --> 01:01:36.370
Dare to bore me.
敢于让我感到无聊。

1317
01:01:36.750 --> 01:01:36.950
That was.
确实是这样。

1318
01:01:37.210 --> 01:01:37.690
Dare to bore me.
敢于让我感到无聊。

1319
01:01:37.790 --> 01:01:38.810
It was so scary.
当时太吓人了。

1320
01:01:38.990 --> 01:01:40.070
It's so scary.
真的太吓人了。

1321
01:01:40.070 --> 01:01:41.910
Oh, because you want to just go for the fences.
哦，因为你总是想全力以赴。

1322
01:01:42.590 --> 01:01:43.230
It's juSt.
这只是。

1323
01:01:43.310 --> 01:01:45.850
It's so hard to just have restraint.
保持克制真的太难了。

1324
01:01:46.430 --> 01:01:51.550
That's like, for me, the hardest thing about acting is just holding in silence.
对我来说，演戏最难的就是保持沉默。

1325
01:01:51.910 --> 01:01:54.470
You really are working with people that are all doing it.
你合作的那些人真的都在这么做。

1326
01:01:54.550 --> 01:01:55.750
And it's so fucking funny.
而且这真的太他妈搞笑了。

1327
01:01:56.110 --> 01:01:57.270
It's amazing.
太棒了。

1328
01:01:57.630 --> 01:02:00.810
It's just amazing, amazing thing to have been a part of.
能参与其中，这真是一件了不起、太了不起的事情。

1329
01:02:00.910 --> 01:02:03.250
It just, I still can't believe it.
我至今仍觉得难以置信。

1330
01:02:03.390 --> 01:02:05.430
And just what it means to people too.
而且它对人们的意义也非同寻常。

1331
01:02:05.650 --> 01:02:06.850
Like, that's so cool.
这真的很酷。

1332
01:02:06.850 --> 01:02:12.090
I know that the office has gotten people through hard times in their lives.
我知道《办公室》陪很多人度过了人生中的艰难时刻。

1333
01:02:12.870 --> 01:02:21.970
And, you know, once in, long ago, I fell down a set of stairs in New York at Budokan.
你知道，很久以前，我在纽约的武道馆摔下了一段楼梯。

1334
01:02:22.050 --> 01:02:23.730
It was during like an NBC event.
当时是在参加一个NBC的活动。

1335
01:02:24.030 --> 01:02:25.990
I was there with Fred Armisen, actually.
其实当时弗雷德·阿米森也在场。

1336
01:02:26.370 --> 01:02:31.430
And I fell down this set of stairs and I broke my back in four places.
我从楼梯上摔了下来，背部骨折了四处。

1337
01:02:31.670 --> 01:02:32.270
Oh, Jesus.
天哪。

1338
01:02:32.270 --> 01:02:38.590
And while I was recovering, I watched the Larry Sanders show.
在康复期间，我看了《拉里·桑德斯秀》。

1339
01:02:39.350 --> 01:02:42.610
And it was like better than any pain medicine.
那比任何止痛药都管用。

1340
01:02:43.530 --> 01:02:49.030
So like the fact that I can, like, I can be part of something that is that for other people.
所以，能参与到一部对别人有同样意义的作品中，这种感觉……

1341
01:02:49.030 --> 01:02:53.230
Like, I know what it means to have a thing that like gets you through something.
我深知拥有一部能陪你度过难关的作品意味着什么。

1342
01:02:53.470 --> 01:02:54.510
It's really cool.
这真的很酷。

1343
01:02:54.510 --> 01:03:01.490
Wow, that's full circle because I believe that Ricky Gervais felt like he was influenced by the Larry Sanders show.
哇，这真是个完美的闭环，因为我相信瑞奇·热维斯也深受《拉里·桑德斯秀》的影响。

1344
01:03:02.250 --> 01:03:09.010
And then he does the British office and then you go to the American office and then you break your back and then you're watching Larry Sanders.
然后他制作了英版《办公室》，接着你去了美版《办公室》，然后你摔断了背，又在看《拉里·桑德斯秀》。

1345
01:03:09.250 --> 01:03:13.030
I don't know where this keeps going, but there's something kind of cool about that.
我不知道这缘分会如何延续，但这其中确实有些很酷的东西。

1346
01:03:14.010 --> 01:03:15.570
That was a show that was magic.
那真是一部充满魔力的剧。

1347
01:03:15.730 --> 01:03:16.350
We were both on it.
我们俩都参演了。

1348
01:03:16.410 --> 01:03:17.050
Were you on it, David?
你参演了吗，大卫？

1349
01:03:17.430 --> 01:03:18.150
We were on Larry.
我们都演过《拉里》。

1350
01:03:18.150 --> 01:03:25.630
Also, we all worked with Greg Daniels, who is a shout out to him, who's a great writer that obviously SNL.
而且，我们都和格雷格·丹尼尔斯合作过，向他致敬，他是一位伟大的编剧，显然也是《周六夜现场》的编剧。

1351
01:03:25.790 --> 01:03:36.870
I remember when Greg Daniels and Conan O'Brien walked into the offices at SNL, fresh out of Harvard, looked like they were sophomores in high school, little haircuts,
我记得格雷格·丹尼尔斯和柯南·奥布莱恩刚从哈佛毕业走进《周六夜现场》办公室的时候，看起来就像高中二年级的学生，留着小小的发型，

1352
01:03:37.250 --> 01:03:38.750
kind of nervous looking around.
看起来有点紧张，四处张望。

1353
01:03:39.070 --> 01:03:39.990
Yeah, great.
是啊，太棒了。

1354
01:03:40.490 --> 01:03:40.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1355
01:03:41.090 --> 01:03:42.170
And they were roommates.
而且他们还是室友。

1356
01:03:42.490 --> 01:03:43.390
Yeah, I know.
是啊，我知道。

1357
01:03:43.590 --> 01:03:44.550
It's amazing, really.
这真的很神奇。

1358
01:03:46.150 --> 01:03:55.510
You know, the SNL years you liked, it's like we were propped up by guys like that and Bob Odenkirk and Smigel and Downey and Frank.
你知道，你喜欢的那些《周六夜现场》的岁月，就像是我们被像他们那样的人，还有鲍勃·奥登科克、斯米格尔、唐尼和弗兰克这些人支撑着一样。

1359
01:03:55.530 --> 01:03:55.790
Yeah.
是啊。

1360
01:03:56.010 --> 01:03:57.310
There's so many good writers there.
那里有太多优秀的编剧了。

1361
01:03:57.350 --> 01:04:03.470
It's kind of nice when, and I'm sure you just do this, you're not trying to get kudos about it, but if someone says to you later,
当你走进那样的环境时，如果有人后来对你说——我肯定你也会这样做，你并不是为了博取赞美——

1362
01:04:03.470 --> 01:04:09.370
because not everyone is really friendly when you walk into an environment like that, and they'd say, oh, you were so nice to us.
因为并不是每个人在你走进那样的环境时都很友好，但他们会说，哦，你当时对我们真好。

1363
01:04:09.370 --> 01:04:10.150
I go, really?
我说，真的吗？

1364
01:04:10.150 --> 01:04:10.650
I was?
我当时是吗？

1365
01:04:10.790 --> 01:04:12.830
I think I was just like, how are you guys doing or something?
我想我当时可能只是问了句你们好吗之类的吧？

1366
01:04:12.830 --> 01:04:16.690
But some people are like, ah, more competition, we don't need you.
但有些人会觉得，啊，又多了竞争对手，我们不需要你。

1367
01:04:16.830 --> 01:04:19.830
You know, it can be a little cold at SNL.
你知道，在《周六夜现场》可能会有点冷漠。

1368
01:04:19.990 --> 01:04:23.870
No one's really telling you where you should stand or what you should even do.
没人会真正告诉你你应该站在哪里，或者你甚至应该做什么。

1369
01:04:24.350 --> 01:04:25.290
That's what we learned.
这就是我们学到的。

1370
01:04:25.390 --> 01:04:32.630
A lot of people are like, they didn't even know, no one told them anything, you know, about the show, and they just had to figure it out for themselves.
很多人都说，他们甚至不知道，没人告诉他们任何关于节目的事，他们只能自己摸索。

1371
01:04:32.890 --> 01:04:33.430
But anyway.
但不管怎样。

1372
01:04:33.970 --> 01:04:35.590
Well, it's an interesting environment.
嗯，那是一个有趣的环境。

1373
01:04:35.590 --> 01:04:42.210
I got to be on the show as part of Steve Carell's monologue once.
我有幸在史蒂夫·卡瑞尔的独白环节中上过一次节目。

1374
01:04:42.670 --> 01:04:43.550
I remember that.
我记得那件事。

1375
01:04:43.550 --> 01:04:50.570
And I was, I mean, again, like I told you, I'm a Saturday Night Live groupie nerd.
而且我，我是说，再说一次，就像我告诉你的，我是《周六夜现场》的死忠粉。

1376
01:04:50.770 --> 01:04:54.310
And so this was, I don't even remember what I had going on.
所以当时，我甚至不记得我当时在忙什么。

1377
01:04:54.310 --> 01:04:55.790
I got like 24 hours notice.
我大概提前24小时收到的通知。

1378
01:04:55.990 --> 01:04:57.490
Do you want to come fly in?
你想飞过来吗？

1379
01:04:57.570 --> 01:04:58.430
And I was like, yes.
我说，愿意。

1380
01:04:58.670 --> 01:05:00.090
I came in on a red eye.
我坐红眼航班来的。

1381
01:05:00.290 --> 01:05:01.230
I was like, anything.
我当时想，什么都行。

1382
01:05:01.770 --> 01:05:05.730
And to be in the bowels, to like get to be there for the rehearsal.
能深入内部，能参加排练。

1383
01:05:06.110 --> 01:05:10.670
And then how like, oh my God, it really does change from the rehearsal.
然后发现，天哪，它真的和排练时完全不一样。

1384
01:05:10.970 --> 01:05:12.090
That was nuts.
那真是太疯狂了。

1385
01:05:12.090 --> 01:05:14.150
And just, it was so scary.
而且，那太吓人了。

1386
01:05:14.550 --> 01:05:16.230
And my line changed.
我的台词改了。

1387
01:05:16.310 --> 01:05:17.610
And then the cue card changed.
提示卡也改了。

1388
01:05:17.810 --> 01:05:20.510
And then how we went, all went into Lauren's office.
然后我们所有人都去了洛恩的办公室。

1389
01:05:20.510 --> 01:05:26.170
And you're like sitting on the floor, like waiting to hear like what things made it and what didn't.
你坐在地板上，等着听哪些段子留下了，哪些被砍掉了。

1390
01:05:26.170 --> 01:05:28.130
And I couldn't believe I was invited.
我简直不敢相信我被邀请了。

1391
01:05:28.330 --> 01:05:33.410
I was like, I'm just the, I just have like one sentence in the opening monologue.
我当时想，我只是，我只是在开场独白里有一句台词而已。

1392
01:05:33.530 --> 01:05:36.270
But I was like privy to all of the inner workings.
但我却得以窥见所有的幕后运作。

1393
01:05:36.330 --> 01:05:38.110
It was so awesome.
那真是太棒了。

1394
01:05:38.490 --> 01:05:39.070
It is.
确实是。

1395
01:05:39.070 --> 01:05:47.870
And then that night at the after party, I held Lorne Michaels' focus for 30 solid minutes.
那天晚上的庆功宴上，我独占了洛恩·迈克尔斯的注意力整整30分钟。

1396
01:05:48.070 --> 01:05:48.530
Whoa.
哇。

1397
01:05:48.970 --> 01:05:57.130
And I still to this day, it is one of my best like small talk moments ever.
直到今天，这仍是我有史以来最棒的闲聊时刻之一。

1398
01:05:58.450 --> 01:06:00.550
Because I'd met him many times.
因为我以前见过他很多次。

1399
01:06:00.550 --> 01:06:05.990
I had come and I saw when Christina Applegate hosted and when Jon Hamm hosted, I came as our gueSt.
我曾来看过克里斯蒂娜·艾伯盖特和乔·哈姆主持的节目，我是作为嘉宾来的。

1400
01:06:05.990 --> 01:06:09.590
And I would sit and I would run into him and shake his hand and all this sort of stuff.
我会坐在那里，遇到他，和他握手，诸如此类。

1401
01:06:09.910 --> 01:06:20.870
And, but for whatever reason, at this particular after party, I got in a whole chat with him about how I like to prep for the apocalypse.
而且，不管出于什么原因，在那场庆功派对上，我和他聊了很久关于我如何为世界末日做准备的话题。

1402
01:06:21.430 --> 01:06:24.130
And he was very interested in this topic.
他对这个话题非常感兴趣。

1403
01:06:24.630 --> 01:06:27.990
And we spoke for like a solid 25 minutes.
我们足足聊了25分钟。

1404
01:06:27.990 --> 01:06:28.370
Wow.
哇。

1405
01:06:28.530 --> 01:06:30.130
And I wanted to keep talking to him.
我当时还想继续和他聊下去。

1406
01:06:30.230 --> 01:06:31.170
I wanted to keep going.
我想继续聊。

1407
01:06:31.170 --> 01:06:33.990
But I knew that I had to say goodbye.
但我知道我必须告辞了。

1408
01:06:34.430 --> 01:06:34.730
Yeah.
是啊。

1409
01:06:35.210 --> 01:06:36.650
I, and I did it.
我，我做到了。

1410
01:06:36.790 --> 01:06:38.550
I left at the right time.
我在合适的时机离开了。

1411
01:06:39.030 --> 01:06:40.710
And I'm so proud of myself.
我为自己感到骄傲。

1412
01:06:41.730 --> 01:06:42.330
That's interesting.
真有意思。

1413
01:06:42.490 --> 01:06:43.830
And now I never want to speak to him again.
现在我再也不想和他说话了。

1414
01:06:43.850 --> 01:06:45.170
I will never speak to him again.
我再也不会和他说话了。

1415
01:06:45.350 --> 01:06:46.250
I will not ruin it.
我不会破坏这种感觉。

1416
01:06:46.450 --> 01:06:48.170
Six years there, I didn't get 30 total.
在那里待了六年，我总共都没聊够30分钟。

1417
01:06:49.050 --> 01:06:52.710
It was, I'm telling you, I'll never, I never ever want to run into him again.
我跟你说，我再也不想、绝对不想再碰到他了。

1418
01:06:52.830 --> 01:06:54.470
That was a good subject matter for him.
那对他来说是个很好的话题。

1419
01:06:54.630 --> 01:06:55.850
Something that he would be like.
那种他会觉得……

1420
01:06:56.330 --> 01:06:57.490
Just doesn't talk about every day.
平时不会聊到的东西。

1421
01:06:57.490 --> 01:07:03.650
You first have to make sure that you procure a fair amount of water in the event of apocalypse.
你首先得确保在世界末日来临时，储备了足够多的水。

1422
01:07:04.610 --> 01:07:05.790
I put Triscuits down there.
我在下面放了些脆饼干。

1423
01:07:05.790 --> 01:07:06.970
I mean, did he respond at all?
我是说，他有回应吗？

1424
01:07:07.130 --> 01:07:11.750
I mean, you really talked about your preparation for the apocalypse, like for 30 minutes straight.
我的意思是，你真的连续聊了30分钟关于你如何为末日做准备的话题。

1425
01:07:12.830 --> 01:07:14.330
For a good amount of time.
聊了很长一段时间。

1426
01:07:14.470 --> 01:07:17.630
But then we also talked about the movie The Edge, which is my favorite movie.
但后来我们也聊到了电影《势不两立》，那是我最喜欢的电影。

1427
01:07:18.070 --> 01:07:20.190
And, you know, it's a survivalist movie.
你知道的，那是一部生存题材的电影。

1428
01:07:20.330 --> 01:07:23.010
I love movies where people have to survive things.
我喜欢看人们必须在困境中求生的电影。

1429
01:07:23.270 --> 01:07:24.590
I've seen it at least five times.
我至少看了五遍。

1430
01:07:24.590 --> 01:07:29.670
And that's a movie, and we told Alec Baldwin that, that friends come over or relatives,
那是一部电影，我们还告诉亚历克·鲍德温，当朋友或亲戚来家里时，

1431
01:07:29.930 --> 01:07:30.890
oh, let's watch a movie.
哦，我们看部电影吧。

1432
01:07:31.150 --> 01:07:33.350
And once in a while, I'll go, have you seen The Edge?
偶尔我会问，你看过《势不两立》吗？

1433
01:07:33.430 --> 01:07:33.870
They go, no.
他们说，没看过。

1434
01:07:33.990 --> 01:07:38.810
I go, it's just kind of a surefire, great, entertaining film.
我说，那绝对是一部精彩又好看的电影。

1435
01:07:38.890 --> 01:07:39.670
No one could not like it.
没人会不喜欢它。

1436
01:07:39.670 --> 01:07:41.950
Dana, what one man can do, another can do.
达娜，一个人能做到的事，另一个人也能做到。

1437
01:07:43.090 --> 01:07:44.110
That's from the movie.
那是电影里的台词。

1438
01:07:44.130 --> 01:07:46.090
What one man can do, another can do.
一个人能做到的事，另一个人也能做到。

1439
01:07:46.190 --> 01:07:48.730
I'm telling you, that's gotten me through, like, big life moments.
我跟你说，这句话帮我度过了人生中的许多重大时刻。

1440
01:07:48.910 --> 01:07:49.690
I love this movie.
我爱这部电影。

1441
01:07:49.690 --> 01:07:57.770
And so we talked about The Edge, which ended up leading into survivalist stuff, into prepping.
所以我们聊了《势不两立》，这引出了生存主义的话题，聊到了末日准备。

1442
01:07:58.070 --> 01:08:01.630
And he was really interested in my currency plans.
他对我的货币计划非常感兴趣。

1443
01:08:01.810 --> 01:08:05.370
Like, what were my plans for currency during the apocalypse?
比如，我在世界末日期间的货币计划是什么？

1444
01:08:05.690 --> 01:08:07.410
Did I have gold bars?
我有金条吗？

1445
01:08:07.810 --> 01:08:08.950
Like, and you know what?
而且你知道吗？

1446
01:08:09.170 --> 01:08:10.790
To be honest, I hadn't thought of it.
老实说，我还没想过这个问题。

1447
01:08:10.970 --> 01:08:12.570
I hadn't gotten as far as currency.
我还没考虑到货币这一步。

1448
01:08:13.710 --> 01:08:18.450
I was funny, when I was there in the fall doing Biden, just behind his decks, I saw this whole
真有意思，秋天我在那儿模仿拜登的时候，就在他的桌子后面，我看到了这个大大的

1449
01:08:18.450 --> 01:08:21.390
duffel bag, you know, it was really big, you know?
行李袋，你知道，真的很大，对吧？

1450
01:08:21.590 --> 01:08:25.930
And then when he left to go to the bathroom, it was just all this survival stuff in there.
然后当他去洗手间的时候，里面装的全是生存装备。

1451
01:08:26.030 --> 01:08:30.390
He goes by and he pushes a wall and it spins around and it disappears down a slide.
他走过去推了一堵墙，墙就转了起来，然后顺着滑梯消失了。

1452
01:08:30.630 --> 01:08:31.150
Oh, I want to be ready.
噢，我想做好准备。

1453
01:08:31.150 --> 01:08:33.930
He was influenced by my prep.
他受了我的预科班影响。

1454
01:08:34.150 --> 01:08:36.190
Tony Hopkins had that line, right?
那句台词是托尼·霍普金斯说的，对吧？

1455
01:08:36.290 --> 01:08:38.010
One man can do, another man can do.
一个人能做到的，另一个人也能做到。

1456
01:08:38.070 --> 01:08:38.990
Is that Tony Hopkins?
那是托尼·霍普金斯吗？

1457
01:08:39.810 --> 01:08:40.790
Yes, correct.
是的，没错。

1458
01:08:40.790 --> 01:08:44.990
And Al, Al Baldwin was great in that.
还有艾尔，艾尔·鲍德温在里面演得真棒。

1459
01:08:45.130 --> 01:08:45.790
So was Tony.
托尼也是。

1460
01:08:46.550 --> 01:08:48.610
Oh, I love when people change names.
噢，我喜欢人们改名字。

1461
01:08:49.150 --> 01:08:51.110
Jen Jen was great on our podcaSt.
珍·珍在我们播客上表现得太棒了。

1462
01:08:51.250 --> 01:08:51.630
Jen Fisher.
珍·费舍尔。

1463
01:08:52.090 --> 01:08:52.970
Does anyone call you Jen?
有人叫你珍吗？

1464
01:08:53.590 --> 01:08:55.130
No, no one's ever called me Jen.
没有，从来没人叫过我珍。

1465
01:08:56.050 --> 01:08:59.410
Well, get ready for it, because we have a lot of followers.
好吧，做好心理准备吧，因为我们有很多粉丝。

1466
01:08:59.590 --> 01:09:02.150
By the way, people may not know, but we're on the same network.
顺便说一下，大家可能不知道，我们是在同一个网络平台。

1467
01:09:02.310 --> 01:09:03.750
It's almost like television now.
现在简直就像电视节目一样。

1468
01:09:04.090 --> 01:09:04.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1469
01:09:04.230 --> 01:09:05.270
So that's kind of cool.
所以这挺酷的。

1470
01:09:05.630 --> 01:09:07.370
This is jury duty for Jen.
这是珍的陪审义务。

1471
01:09:07.370 --> 01:09:10.470
And I, just for people who are watching this or might want to see it.
还有我，只是为了那些正在看或者可能想看的人说明一下。

1472
01:09:10.470 --> 01:09:12.670
So are you in a studio somewhere?
所以你是在某个演播室里吗？

1473
01:09:13.230 --> 01:09:17.210
Yeah, I'm at your New York studios.
是的，我在你们纽约的演播室。

1474
01:09:17.570 --> 01:09:20.390
Yeah, I'm here in New York this week.
没错，我这周在纽约。

1475
01:09:20.430 --> 01:09:22.950
And so I came into the New York studio.
所以我来到了纽约演播室。

1476
01:09:23.230 --> 01:09:27.690
And are you and Angela usually in different places when you do the podcast and sometimes together?
你们做播客时，通常是分处两地，还是有时在一起？

1477
01:09:28.030 --> 01:09:28.570
Or always together?
还是说一直都在一起？

1478
01:09:28.570 --> 01:09:30.150
No, we're usually together.
不，我们通常都在一起。

1479
01:09:30.950 --> 01:09:35.110
Odyssey, our company that we both work for, has a studio in Hollywood.
我们共同效力的公司Odyssey在好莱坞有个演播室。

1480
01:09:35.110 --> 01:09:37.530
And we usually record there in person together.
我们通常在那里面对面录制。

1481
01:09:37.990 --> 01:09:40.170
And you guys are all set up at home.
你们在家里都布置好了。

1482
01:09:40.370 --> 01:09:42.170
Like, you guys have cool setups.
你们的设备看起来很酷。

1483
01:09:43.030 --> 01:09:43.470
We do.
确实。

1484
01:09:43.710 --> 01:09:44.250
It's going in person.
这是面对面录制的。

1485
01:09:44.530 --> 01:09:45.390
We've been going in person.
我们一直都是面对面录制的。

1486
01:09:45.530 --> 01:09:45.580
I don't know.
我不知道。

1487
01:09:45.630 --> 01:09:48.710
I kind of feel like I need a background or something.
我总觉得我需要个背景什么的。

1488
01:09:49.050 --> 01:09:50.310
It changes a lot.
这经常变。

1489
01:09:50.450 --> 01:09:53.850
When I was doing SNL, I was just in a hotel room doing it.
我做《周六夜现场》的时候，就是在一个酒店房间里录的。

1490
01:09:54.030 --> 01:09:57.270
That's one of the advantages of this, is that you can do it remotely.
